# Project Architecture

## Backend Layers (Hexagonal / Modular-Monolith)

| Layer | Path | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| API | `backend/app/api/` | FastAPI routers + WebSocket endpoints |
| Application | `backend/app/application/` | Use-case services (`AnalysisService`, `AuthService`) + Pydantic schemas |
| Domain | `backend/app/domain/` | `DomainEvent` dataclass (thin domain layer) |
| Infrastructure | `backend/app/infrastructure/` | DB (SQLAlchemy async), Docker gateway, Redis event bus, subprocess tools |

**Strict rule:** API layer never imports SQLAlchemy directly — always go through repositories and services.

## Async Job Pipeline

1. API router receives upload → creates DB job → enqueues `arq` task via Redis
2. Worker picks up task → runs `AnalysisService.run_job_with_plugins()`
3. Worker publishes `DomainEvent`s to Redis pub/sub
4. WebSocket endpoints subscribe to channels and stream events to the browser

## Redis Channel Naming

- `user:{user_id}:events` — all events for a user
- `job:{job_id}:events` — events scoped to a specific job
- `container:{container_id}:metrics` — container CPU/memory metrics
- `user:{user_id}:container:{container_id}:metrics` — user-scoped container metrics

## Plugin System

Plugins live in `backend/app/plugins/`. Each extends `BasePlugin` (single `async run(context) → dict`). The `PLUGIN_MAP` in `registry.py` maps names to classes. Worker tasks select plugins by job type:
- **Dockerfile**: hadolint, security_scanner, resource_estimation
- **Compose**: compose_validator, compose_runnability, security_scanner, resource_estimation
- **Project archive**: dynamic subset based on detected files

## Docker-in-Docker (DinD)

Worker uses `DOCKER_HOST=tcp://dind:2375` to reach an isolated DinD sidecar. All `docker-compose` subprocess calls execute inside the worker container — never the host socket.

## Frontend

React 19 SPA (`frontend/src/`). Pages in `src/pages/`, components in `src/components/`, Radix-based primitives in `src/components/ui/`. All API calls go through `src/utils/api.ts`. Auth context in `src/auth/AuthProvider.tsx`.
